---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="CmdImpact" description="Paste a terminal command from ChatGPT, Claude, Codex, Copilot or GitHub and see what it may install, download, delete, overwrite or expose before you run it.">
	<section class="hero">
		<div class="shell hero-grid">
			<div class="hero-copy">
				<p class="kicker">A pause button for copy-paste coding</p>
				<h1>Spot common <em>command risks</em> before you run it.</h1>
				<p>Paste a command from an AI answer or GitHub. CmdImpact checks for common install, download, delete, administrator, network and exposed-secret patterns—without running anything.</p>
				<div class="source-row" aria-label="Common command sources"><span>ChatGPT</span><span>Claude</span><span>Codex</span><span>GitHub</span><span>Copilot</span><span>Gemini</span></div>
				<div class="hero-note">
					<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3 4.5 6v5.5c0 4.8 3.2 7.8 7.5 9.5 4.3-1.7 7.5-4.7 7.5-9.5V6L12 3Z"/><path d="m8.5 12 2.1 2.1 4.9-5"/></svg>
					<span><strong>Your text stays here.</strong> The checker runs inside this browser tab and the checker page loads no ads.</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<section id="checker" class="checker-card" aria-labelledby="checker-title">
				<div class="terminal-bar"><span class="terminal-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>cmdimpact / local-check</span><span>v1</span></div>
				<form id="command-form" class="checker-form">
					<div class="checker-label"><label id="checker-title" for="command-input">Paste a command</label><span id="character-count">0 / 50,000</span></div>
					<p class="checker-help">Paste only the command or short code block you were told to run—not the surrounding explanation. Replace real passwords, API keys, tokens, private URLs and confidential data with placeholders first.</p>
					<textarea id="command-input" class="command-input" name="command" maxlength="50000" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Example:&#10;curl -fsSL https://example.com/install.sh | sh" required></textarea>
					<div class="example-row"><span>Try:</span><button class="example-chip" type="button" data-example="remote">curl | sh</button><button class="example-chip" type="button" data-example="delete">rm -rf</button><button class="example-chip" type="button" data-example="powershell">iwr | iex</button><button class="example-chip" type="button" data-example="package">npm install</button></div>
					<p id="input-error" class="input-error" role="alert" hidden></p>
					<div class="checker-actions"><p>Nothing is uploaded, saved or run.</p><button class="check-button" type="submit">Check this command →</button></div>
				</form>
				<section id="results" class="results" aria-live="polite" hidden>
					<div class="result-head"><span id="verdict-mark" class="verdict-mark" aria-hidden="true">!</span><div><h2 id="verdict-title"></h2><p id="verdict-detail"></p></div><span id="result-shell" class="result-shell"></span></div>
					<div id="finding-list" class="result-body"></div>
					<p class="result-limit">Pattern check only: CmdImpact cannot inspect downloaded code, custom aliases, variables or what programs do internally. It does not verify that a command is safe.</p>
					<div class="result-tools"><p>Paste these questions into the AI that gave you the command. Review any replacement too.</p><button id="copy-fix" class="result-button" type="button">Copy questions for the AI</button><button id="clear-check" class="result-button" type="button">Check another command</button></div>
				</section>
			</section>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-tint">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="section-heading"><div><p class="kicker">Why it exists</p><h2>AI moves fast. A terminal moves faster.</h2></div><p>A polished answer can still ask for more access than the task needs, install the wrong package or hide a destructive step inside a one-liner.</p></div>
			<div class="problem-grid">
				<article class="story-card"><span class="card-index">01 / RECEIVE</span><h3>An AI gives you a command.</h3><p>It may come from ChatGPT, Claude, Codex, Copilot, Gemini, a GitHub issue or a README.</p></article>
				<article class="story-card"><span class="card-index">02 / PAUSE</span><h3>You paste it here first.</h3><p>CmdImpact reads the text locally. It never starts a shell, downloads code or touches your files.</p></article>
				<article class="story-card is-impact"><span class="card-index">03 / UNDERSTAND</span><h3>You see what needs checking.</h3><p>Known download, install, deletion, overwrite, administrator, network and exposed-secret patterns are called out in plain English.</p></article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="shell proof-panel">
			<div class="proof-copy"><p class="kicker">Evidence, not a score</p><h2>A result you can act on.</h2><p>No mysterious 83/100 badge. Every warning names the pattern, shows the relevant line and explains what to verify before continuing.</p><a class="button secondary" href="/methodology/">See every check →</a></div>
			<div class="proof-receipt" aria-label="Example CmdImpact result">
				<div class="receipt-label"><span>IMPACT RECEIPT</span><span>BASH · 3 ACTIONS</span></div>
				<p class="receipt-verdict">PAUSE — REVIEW FIRST</p>
				<div class="receipt-list"><div><span>!</span><p><strong>Remote content may execute directly</strong><small>The download is passed straight to a shell.</small></p></div><div><span>↓</span><p><strong>Network download</strong><small>Confirm the source and inspect the file first.</small></p></div><div><span>#</span><p><strong>Elevated privileges</strong><small>System-wide changes may be possible.</small></p></div></div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-tint" id="how-it-works">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="section-heading"><div><p class="kicker">Focused first release</p><h2>Useful today. Honest about its limits.</h2></div><p>CmdImpact finds known patterns; it cannot understand custom aliases, inspect your computer or promise a command is safe.</p></div>
			<div class="feature-grid">
				<article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">↓</span><h3>Downloads and installs</h3><p>Recognizes common curl, wget, PowerShell, npm, npx, pip and system package commands.</p></article>
				<article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">×</span><h3>File-changing actions</h3><p>Highlights known deletion, recursive deletion, overwrite and hard-reset patterns.</p></article>
				<article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">#</span><h3>Access and exposure</h3><p>Calls out elevation, network activity and credential-shaped values embedded in commands.</p></article>
			</div>
			<div class="supported-row" aria-label="Initial support"><span>Bash / sh</span><span>PowerShell</span><span>npm / npx</span><span>pip / pipx</span><span>Common package managers</span><span>50 KB local input</span></div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="section-heading"><div><p class="kicker">Learn the risky patterns</p><h2>Short guides for commands AI often suggests.</h2></div><a href="/guides/">View all guides →</a></div>
			<div class="guide-grid">
				<article class="guide-card"><p class="kicker">Bash · 4 min</p><h3>Why “curl | sh” deserves a pause</h3><p>Understand the download-to-execution chain and a more inspectable workflow.</p><a href="/guides/curl-pipe-shell/">Read the guide →</a></article>
				<article class="guide-card"><p class="kicker">PowerShell · 4 min</p><h3>What “iwr | iex” does</h3><p>See why this compact installer pattern can hide the code your machine runs.</p><a href="/guides/powershell-iwr-iex/">Read the guide →</a></article>
				<article class="guide-card"><p class="kicker">Packages · 5 min</p><h3>Check a package invented by AI</h3><p>Package existence is evidence—not proof of ownership, quality or safety.</p><a href="/guides/check-ai-package/">Read the guide →</a></article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
	import { analyzeCommand, type CommandFinding, type CommandReport } from '../lib/command-check';

	const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#command-form');
	const input = document.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('#command-input');
	const count = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#character-count');
	const error = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#input-error');
	const results = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#results');
	const title = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#verdict-title');
	const detail = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#verdict-detail');
	const mark = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#verdict-mark');
	const shell = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#result-shell');
	const list = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#finding-list');
	const copyButton = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#copy-fix');
	const clearButton = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#clear-check');
	let currentReport: CommandReport | undefined;

	const examples: Record<string, string> = {
		remote: 'curl -fsSL https://example.com/install.sh | sh',
		delete: 'rm -rf ./generated',
		powershell: 'iwr https://example.com/setup.ps1 | iex',
		package: 'npm install example-package',
	};

	const findingIcons: Record<CommandFinding['category'], string> = {
		install: '+', download: '↓', delete: '×', overwrite: '↻', elevation: '#', network: '↗', secret: '*',
	};

	function setText(element: Element | null, value: string) {
		if (element) element.textContent = value;
	}

	function findingElement(finding: CommandFinding) {
		const item = document.createElement('article');
		item.className = `finding ${finding.severity}`;
		const icon = document.createElement('span');
		icon.className = 'finding-icon';
		icon.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
		icon.textContent = findingIcons[finding.category];
		const body = document.createElement('div');
		const heading = document.createElement('div');
		heading.className = 'finding-title';
		const name = document.createElement('h3');
		name.textContent = finding.title;
		const severity = document.createElement('span');
		severity.className = 'severity';
		severity.textContent = `${finding.severity === 'high' ? 'STOP & CHECK' : 'CHECK'} · LINE ${finding.line}`;
		const description = document.createElement('p');
		description.textContent = finding.detail;
		const evidence = document.createElement('code');
		evidence.textContent = finding.evidence;
		heading.append(name, severity);
		body.append(heading, description, evidence);
		item.append(icon, body);
		return item;
	}

	function render(report: CommandReport) {
		if (!results || !list) return;
		currentReport = report;
		results.dataset.risk = report.risk;
		const highCount = report.findings.filter((finding) => finding.severity === 'high').length;
		const copy = report.risk === 'high'
			? ['Do not run yet', `${report.findings.length} supported pattern${report.findings.length === 1 ? '' : 's'} matched, including ${highCount} urgent warning${highCount === 1 ? '' : 's'}.`]
			: report.risk === 'review'
				? ['Check before running', `${report.findings.length} supported pattern${report.findings.length === 1 ? '' : 's'} matched. Confirm each one.`]
				: ['No supported warning found', 'CmdImpact did not verify this command. Read it and confirm its purpose.'];
		setText(title, copy[0]);
		setText(detail, copy[1]);
		setText(mark, report.risk === 'high' ? '!' : report.risk === 'review' ? '?' : '·');
		setText(shell, report.shell === 'unknown' ? '' : report.shell);
		if (shell) shell.hidden = report.shell === 'unknown';
		list.replaceChildren();
		if (report.findings.length) report.findings.forEach((finding) => list.append(findingElement(finding)));
		results.hidden = false;
		results.scrollIntoView({ behavior: matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
	}

	input?.addEventListener('input', () => {
		setText(count, `${input.value.length.toLocaleString()} / 50,000`);
		if (error) error.hidden = true;
	});

	document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-example]').forEach((button) => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
		if (!input) return;
		input.value = examples[button.dataset.example ?? ''] ?? '';
		input.dispatchEvent(new Event('input'));
		input.focus();
	}));

	form?.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
		event.preventDefault();
		if (!input || !input.value.trim()) {
			if (error) { error.textContent = 'Paste at least one command to check.'; error.hidden = false; }
			input?.focus();
			return;
		}
		render(analyzeCommand(input.value));
	});

	copyButton?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
		if (!currentReport) return;
		const command = currentReport.actions.map((action) => `- Line ${action.line}: ${action.evidence}`).join('\n');
		const findings = currentReport.findings.map((finding) => `- ${finding.title} (line ${finding.line}): ${finding.detail} Evidence: ${finding.evidence}`).join('\n');
		const request = `Please review these redacted command excerpts without executing anything:\n\n${command || '- No command excerpt available.'}\n\n${findings ? `CmdImpact patterns:\n${findings}` : 'No supported CmdImpact warning matched. Explain the command line by line, identify anything the static check may have missed, and propose a version with the smallest necessary access.'}\n\nExplain every remaining side effect. If you propose a replacement, remind me to review it before running it.`;
		try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(request); copyButton.textContent = 'Questions copied'; }
		catch { copyButton.textContent = 'Copy unavailable'; }
		setTimeout(() => { copyButton.textContent = 'Copy questions for the AI'; }, 1800);
	});

	clearButton?.addEventListener('click', () => {
		if (!input || !results) return;
		input.value = '';
		input.dispatchEvent(new Event('input'));
		results.hidden = true;
		currentReport = undefined;
		input.focus();
	});
</script>
